# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Melarium Frontend — environment variables
#
# Development:
#   Copy to .env.local and adjust. Vite picks it up automatically.
#   .env.local is git-ignored so secrets stay out of version control.
#
# Production (VPS):
#   Nothing to set. nginx serves the built SPA and reverse-proxies /api to the
#   backend on the same origin, so the built-in relative default already works.
#   See docs/deployment.md.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Full URL of the backend API (including the /api suffix).
#
# Leave this UNSET in both dev and production — the code defaults to the relative
# '/api' (see src/core/services/apiClient.ts), which the Vite dev proxy handles
# locally and nginx handles in production.
#
# Only set it to point the SPA at a backend on a different origin — e.g. running
# the frontend locally against the live API. That also means CORS: the target's
# AllowedOrigins must list this frontend's origin.
#VITE_API_URL=https://melarium.app/api
